<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net48</TargetFramework>
		<PlatformTarget>AnyCPU</PlatformTarget>
		<ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>disable</Nullable>
		<AssemblyName>Skyline.DataMiner.Dev.Utils.Solutions.SatOps.Common</AssemblyName>
		<RootNamespace>Skyline.DataMiner.SDM.SatOps.Common</RootNamespace>
		<Copyright>Copyright © 2026</Copyright>
		<PackageTags>Skyline;DataMiner</PackageTags>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://skyline.be</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>True</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
		<PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<Authors>SkylineCommunications</Authors>
		<Company>Skyline Communications</Company>
		<Description>DevPack for the SatOps Solution</Description>
		<Version>0.0.22-alpha</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>Repackaged (0.0.22-alpha): version bump/repack of the 0.0.21-alpha slot-name booking fixes (no functional changes). Fixed (0.0.21-alpha): slot name was not shown on the reservation node right after booking (it only appeared after the first resource swap). AddSlotNameProperty now has an overload that anchors the slot-name property (SubID) to an explicitly supplied transponder node id, so the booking flow can anchor the name to the node it is configuring instead of re-deriving it via GetFirstNodeId after the fact. The existing parameterless-node overload delegates to it using the reservation's single transponder node. Fixed (0.0.20-alpha): a second resource swap crashed the node-config data source with "Sequence contains more than one element". Duplicate slot-name property records (same reservation/job id) could accumulate across swaps; the node-config reads them with Single(), which throws on duplicates. FindSlotNameProperty is now duplicate-safe and self-healing: it collapses multiple records for a reservation to one canonical record (preferring one that still carries a slot value) and deletes the rest, so GetSlotName/AddSlotNameProperty/RefreshSlotNameNodeLink always resolve to a single property. Fixed: the slot-name property (SlcProperties, scope "MediaOps") was orphaned after a resource swap. It is keyed by job id + node id (SubID) and read per node by MediaOps scheduling, but a swap replaces the JobResourceNode with a new id, leaving the property pointing at the removed node. AddSlotNameProperty now refreshes SubID to the current node on update, TransponderRangeReservations.Update re-anchors the property after a transponder change, and new GetSlotName / RefreshSlotNameNodeLink members let the resource-swap flow re-point the slot name to the swapped-in node. Previous fix (0.0.18-alpha): Create drives the job Draft->Tentative (Jobs.SaveAsTentative) so the transponder slot is reserved; MediaOps.Plan aligned to 1.7.0-alpha003 (Plan / Plan.Automation / Plan.GQI coherent) to avoid "job type is out of range".</PackageReleaseNotes>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
		<None Include="LICENSE.txt" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
		<None Include="nuget\Icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.4" />
		<PackageReference Include="Skyline.DataMiner.CICD.CSharpAnalysis.Analyzer" Version="2.1.2">
			<IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
		</PackageReference>
		<PackageReference Include="Skyline.DataMiner.Dev.Utils.SDM.Abstractions" Version="1.0.1" />
		<PackageReference Include="Skyline.DataMiner.Dev.Utils.Solutions.MediaOps.Plan" Version="1.7.0-alpha003" />
		<PackageReference Include="Skyline.DataMiner.SDM" Version="1.0.1" />
		<PackageReference Include="Skyline.DataMiner.SDM.Registration.Common" Version="2.0.5" />
		<PackageReference Include="Skyline.DataMiner.SDM.SourceGenerator.Runtime" Version="1.0.1" />
		<PackageReference Include="Skyline.DataMiner.Utils.DOM" Version="10.5.2.8" />
		<PackageReference Include="Skyline.DataMiner.Utils.SecureCoding.Analyzers" Version="2.2.3">
			<IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
		</PackageReference>
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
